{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cursor/plugins/pulls/419","id":4616659090,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ_aGvs8AAAABEyygkg","html_url":"https://github.com/cursor/plugins/pull/419","diff_url":"https://github.com/cursor/plugins/pull/419.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cursor/plugins/pull/419.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cursor/plugins/issues/419","number":419,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs(pstack): cut 19 more instructions Opus 5.5 does not need","user":{"login":"poteto","id":1390709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto","html_url":"https://github.com/poteto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/poteto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\n\n#414 cut 15 instructions from pstack's skills that Opus 5.5 follows without the text. This PR cuts 19 more, in 15 files. Most repeat a rule that stays in the same skill or in the mode skill. Each cut held up in A/B runs on tasks that exercise it, with and without the text.\n\n- **Reviewer prompts.** On two diffs with planted issues, interrogate's default panel (Opus 5.5, Sol, and Grok 4.7) found 142 of 154 planted critical and warning issues without the report-less lines, against 139 with them, over 22 reviews per side. Noise rose by 0.83 findings per review on Opus 5.5 and did not rise on Sol or Grok 4.7.\n- **reflect.** The 3-5 cap made reviewers pad a session that held one real learning. Without it, padding over 12 runs fell from 34 items to 14, and recall on a session with eight learnings rose from 47 to 75 of 96.\n- **Playbooks.** Opus 5.5 leads removed a test skip planted in a delegate's diff in every run where a delegate returned code, with and without the review lines. They delegated feature code as often without the spawn reminder.\n- **Principles and tdd.** Tasks on an integration, a phased migration, an ask-or-proceed choice, a large log, and two tdd fixes scored the same or better without the lines.\n\n## Scope\n\n19 cuts in 15 files. Three of them rewrite a line instead of deleting it.\n\n- **interrogate (4).** The nit-padding sentence in the reviewer prompt. The two bullets against style rewrites and hypothetical issues. The rubric's security sentence, rewritten to ask for the traced input path of each finding. The two sentences against nits in the code-quality review.\n- **Playbooks and figure-it-out (6).** \"Review its diff yourself.\" in feature step 4. The spawn reminder in feature step 4 and its two named excuses. \"Review the diff.\" in bugfix step 3. The closing bugfix line about the how + why fan-out. The review sentences in refactoring steps 5 and 6. The audit-the-delegates clause in figure-it-out Phase C.\n- **Principles (6).** The \"Code and features\" list in prove-it-works. The \"Delegation\" block in prove-it-works. The final-verification bullet in outcome-oriented-execution. The \"Reserve questions\" bullet in never-block-on-the-human. The \"Supervision is async\" bullet in never-block-on-the-human. The \"Don't read what you won't use\" bullet in guard-the-context-window.\n- **tdd (2).** The explain-first opening of the impractical-test paragraph, rewritten to keep the list of fallback checks. The weak-signal guardrail.\n- **reflect (1).** The 3-5 cap in the three reviewer prompts, rewritten as \"List each durable learning you find\".\n- **Version 0.15.4.** No changelog file, as in #414.\n\nThe perf-issue playbook keeps its \"Review the diff.\" line, because no A/B task exercised it. No frontmatter, model default, or script changes.\n\n## Blast radius\n\nEvery pstack user gets the shorter skills on update.\n\n- interrogate reviewers report more nits and a little more noise. interrogate's lead-judgment step still filters nits and hypothetical findings before the verdict.\n- On a diff with a shell injection, Anthropic's cyber safeguards refused some first attempts by Claude reviewers, a little more often with the trace-and-show line. A retry succeeded each time.\n- reflect reviewers list every durable learning they find. A rich session can give more items, including a mistake that the parent skill already covers.\n- The playbooks no longer repeat the review rule at each delegation step. The mode skill keeps it. figure-it-out still verifies by inspecting the artifact, never a self-report, and prove-it-works still rejects self-reports as proof.\n- feature step 4 no longer names the two excuses for not delegating. Delegation stays mandatory.\n- When a failing test is impractical, tdd no longer asks for an explanation before the fix. Its final response still states why a failing test could not be shown.\n- Not tested. The playbook and principle runs used Opus 5.5 as the lead, and no other lead model ran. pstack sends code delegates to Grok 4.7 by default. The spawn-reminder runs used longer wording than pstack's two sentences. The reflect runs used Grok 4.7 for the divergent prompt, which pstack runs on Opus 5.5. On the judgment prompt, Opus 5.5 padded less and found more without the cap. The refactoring cut and the bugfix fan-out line rest on few runs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/validate-plugins.mjs` passes.\n- `bun test orch watch-pr` passes 52 of 52. No script changed.\n- No frontmatter changed, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n- No README or guide page restates a removed line.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Documentation-only plugin version bump; behavior may shift slightly (more reflect items, slightly noisier interrogate nits) but core rules remain in parent skills.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Bumps **pstack** to **0.15.4** and trims **19 redundant skill instructions** across 15 markdown files—continuation of the Opus 5.5 A/B work from #414—without changing scripts, frontmatter, or model defaults.\n> \n> **interrogate** loses anti-noise guidance (nit padding, style-only rewrites, hypothetical issues) and shortens code-quality output expectations; the security rubric now **requires tracing the input path** for each security finding instead of only warning against untraced claims.\n> \n> **poteto-mode playbooks** and **figure-it-out** drop repeated “review the delegate’s diff” / spawn-reminder / fan-out lines where the parent **poteto-mode** skill and **prove-it-works** already cover verification; **perf-issue** still says “Review the diff.”\n> \n> **Principle skills** shed duplicate bullets (selective reading, async supervision, ask-only-on-ambiguity, final verification reminder, and the prove-it-works code/delegation checklists).\n> \n> **reflect** replaces the “3–5 learnings” cap with **list each durable learning** in all three reviewer prompts.\n> \n> **tdd** simplifies the impractical-test path (no upfront explain-before-fix) and removes one weak-signal guardrail while keeping evidence reporting in the final response.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 773258b8233e6cc09c1894a76cd855f639281793. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","created_at":"2026-09-23T17:32:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T17:37:18Z","closed_at":"2026-09-23T17:37:18Z","merged_at":"2026-09-23T17:37:18Z","merge_commit_sha":"b0b9c7a0baf8b6aa1d00bf77d4101e577d4ba411","assig